{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794127241,"nonce":"pKi52rXEnVvDILDR0RpBfGLhyQs=","title":"Input and textarea caret, selection and hit-testing ignore letter-spacing, so the caret drifts right of tracked text","message":"GitHub issue 69 (FreeSynergy). The cn stylesheet gives .cn-input and .cn-textarea letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight), so the default cn input draws tracked text. The layout measure path learned letter spacing earlier (a368d49, cfc7347), but the editable widgets still position the caret from text_measure::measure_text(text, font_size), which takes no spacing. Each character adds the difference, so the caret ends up right of the drawn text and the gap grows with the text. Selection highlights and click-to-caret hit-testing use the same measurements.\n\nWhere: every measure_text call in widgets/text_input (edit.rs caret and prefix widths, content.rs caret x) and widgets/text_area (edit.rs prefix width; lines.rs line width, wrap tests, caret x and hit-testing). text_measure::measure_text_with_options already takes letter_spacing, so the primitive exists.\n\nNeeded: resolve the letter spacing the field is drawn with (CSS letter-spacing from the cascade, the same value the text draw uses) once per field, and measure every caret, selection, wrap and hit-test width with it. A test that types text with and without letter-spacing and checks the caret x equals the drawn prefix width.\n\nReporter's workaround: .cn-input, .cn-textarea { letter-spacing: 0 } in app CSS. Not yet reproduced here.","files":null}]}